    "points": [
      {
        "id": "p1",
        "heading": "Practice -er",
        "body": "¿Qué aprendiste ayer sobre esta misma materia?\n\nEscribe aquí:\n____________________\n____________________\n____________________\n\n## Repaso\n\nYesterday you practiced -ar forms with cantar and hablar.\n\nRead the key words slowly.\n\nExplain one idea with your own words.\n\nToday deepen the **-er** family with **comer**. Stem **com-** plus **-o / -es / -e** gives **como**, **comes**, **come**. Try **beber** and **leer** (leo, lees, lee) the same way.\n\nMira este ejemplo. Make food sentences: yo **como** arroz, tú **comes** fruta, él **come** pan. Then swap only the person ending and keep the stem.\n\nPractice: Now it's your turn. Your turn. Write yo / tú / él for comer, beber, and leer. Box every -es ending. Draw one clear symbol or small scene about “Spanish verbs: -ar, -er, and -ir”. Add one label from today's lesson.\n\nCommon mistake: Using -ar endings on -er verbs (tú comas). Present tú for -er is comes.\n\n## Drawing for the image band\nDraw one clear symbol or small scene about “Spanish verbs: -ar, -er, and -ir”. Add one label from today's lesson."
      }
    ],
    "summary": "In this lesson, you will use Spanish verb endings to say who does an action.\n\n## Drawing for the image band\nDraw one clear symbol or small scene about “Spanish verbs: -ar, -er, and -ir”. Add one label from today's lesson.",
    "memoryPhrase": "Spanish families: **-ar** (cantar → canto, cantas, canta), **-er** (comer → como, comes, come), **-ir** (vivir → vivo, vives, vive).",
    "weekRecap": "Spanish families: -ar (cantar), -er (comer), -ir (vivir). Conjugate for yo, tú, and él in the present.",
    "priorDayRecap": "Yesterday you practiced -ar forms with cantar and hablar.",
